# Ulta Beauty, Inc. — Company Research Report

**Date:** September 3, 2026  
**Ticker:** NASDAQ: ULTA  
**Decision:** Watch / Defer

## Business overview

Ulta Beauty is a specialty beauty retailer selling cosmetics, fragrance, skincare, wellness and haircare products, plus salon services, through stores and digital channels. Its model combines a broad range of brands and price points with beauty services. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 1](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

Two features may help Ulta retain customers: its Ulta Beauty Rewards program, which management describes as an important retention and loyalty tool, and a selection of exclusive products and brands. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 1](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

## Recent financial performance

Fiscal 2025 net sales were **$12.393 billion**, up 9.7% from $11.296 billion in fiscal 2024. Comparable sales increased **5.4%**, versus 0.7% in fiscal 2024; the filing attributes fiscal-2025 comparable-sales growth to a 3.3% increase in average ticket and a 2.0% increase in transactions. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 7](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

Operating income was **$1.533 billion** in fiscal 2025, down from $1.565 billion in fiscal 2024. Operating margin was **12.4%**, compared with 13.9% in fiscal 2024 and 15.0% in fiscal 2023. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 7](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

This supports my view that sales momentum is encouraging, but that growth alone does not settle the investment case. I still need to see whether Ulta can sustain growth while protecting margins. **Source: Author judgment, based on the figures above.**

## Financial position

At January 31, 2026, Ulta reported **$424.243 million** of cash and cash equivalents and **$62.287 million** outstanding under its credit facilities. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 8 and Note 13—Debt](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

I view this as a relatively strong financial position. **Source: Author judgment, based on the cited cash and borrowing balances.**

## What looks good

Ulta’s fiscal-2025 sales and comparable-sales growth were meaningfully stronger than fiscal 2024. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 7](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

Its broad assortment across price points, salon services, loyalty program, and exclusive offerings are potential differentiators. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 1](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

## What concerns me

The key concern is that operating income declined despite higher sales, and operating margin fell to 12.4% from 13.9% in fiscal 2024. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 7](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

The beauty market is highly competitive. Ulta identifies department stores, specialty stores, drug stores, mass merchandisers, e-commerce businesses, online marketplaces, and salon chains as competitors. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 1 and Item 1A](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

Consumer demand is also a risk: Ulta states that beauty products and salon services can be discretionary purchases and that inflation or weaker economic conditions could reduce spending. [Source: Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K, Item 1A](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm)

## Performance against Ulta's own history

Ulta's recent results look stronger when compared with the prior year. Fiscal 2024 comparable sales increased only **0.7%**, while fiscal 2025 comparable sales increased **5.4%**. At the same time, operating margin declined from **13.9% in fiscal 2024 to 12.4% in fiscal 2025**, continuing the decline from **15.0% in fiscal 2023**.

This creates a mixed picture for me: sales momentum recovered, but profitability has not recovered at the same pace. **Source: Author judgment, based on the cited filings.**

