## Recent evidence and outlook

Ulta’s second-quarter fiscal 2026 results, released August 27, 2026, provide more recent evidence than the fiscal-2025 10-K. Net sales increased **8.9% to $3.036 billion**, comparable sales increased **3.8%**, operating income increased **10.1%**, and diluted EPS increased **13.3% to $6.55**. [Source: Ulta Beauty, “Ulta Beauty Announces Second Quarter Fiscal 2026 Results and Raises Fiscal 2026 Guidance,” August 27, 2026](https://www.ulta.com/investor/news-events/press-releases/detail/234/ulta-beauty-announces-second-quarter-fiscal-2026-results)

These results make me somewhat more positive because operating income and earnings grew along with sales, which addresses part of my concern about declining annual profitability. However, comparable-sales growth of 3.8% was below the 6.7% reported in the same quarter a year earlier, so I would still watch whether comparable-sales momentum continues. **Source: Author judgment, based on the cited quarterly results.**

Management also raised its fiscal-2026 outlook. It now expects net-sales growth of **6.7%–7.2%**, comparable-sales growth of **3.2%–3.7%**, operating-income growth of **8.3%–9.3%**, and diluted EPS of **$28.70–$29.00**. [Source: Ulta Beauty Q2 Fiscal 2026 Earnings Release, August 27, 2026](https://www.ulta.com/investor/news-events/press-releases/detail/234/ulta-beauty-announces-second-quarter-fiscal-2026-results)

Reuters also reported on August 27, 2026 that Ulta raised its annual sales and profit forecasts after the quarter, citing strategic investments in marketing, product assortments, and store expansion. [Source: Reuters, “Ulta Beauty lifts annual forecasts as marketing, product investments fuel growth,” August 27, 2026](https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/ulta-beauty-raises-annual-sales-profit-forecasts-2026-08-27/)

## Risks, challenges, and advantages

### Risks and challenges

- **Margin pressure:** Operating margin has declined over the last several fiscal years.
- **Competition:** Ulta competes with specialty beauty retailers, mass retailers, department stores, e-commerce businesses, online marketplaces, and salon chains.
- **Consumer spending:** Beauty products and salon services can be discretionary purchases.
- **Execution:** Ulta must convert its growth investments into sustainable earnings and margin improvement.
- **Comparable-sales risk:** I would become less confident if comparable sales declined for multiple periods.

### Advantages

- Fiscal-2025 comparable sales recovered strongly from fiscal 2024.
- Net sales continue to grow.
- Ulta has a broad product assortment, loyalty program, salon services, and exclusive offerings.
- The newest quarterly results show growth in sales, operating income, and EPS.
- Management raised full-year fiscal-2026 guidance.

**Sources:** [Ulta Beauty 2026 Form 10-K](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403568/000110465926035243/ulta-20260131x10k.htm); [Ulta Beauty Q2 Fiscal 2026 Earnings Release](https://www.ulta.com/investor/news-events/press-releases/detail/234/ulta-beauty-announces-second-quarter-fiscal-2026-results)

